\ Annotation trust must stay sound against a lying callee. Under the lock the
\ freeze-time inference trusts `lie`'s declared fixnum output, which proves
\ `.`'s parameter and lets the locked build succeed. At runtime the declared
\ result is a string: the call-site tag check behind output narrowing (and,
\ for inference-proven parameters, the consumer's entry check) traps with a
\ type mismatch before the value reaches unboxed code.

lie: ( -- result: fixnum ) [ "oops" ] ;

lie .
